b1 is a text with value "Dates and Time", size 40, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.03em", lineheight "1.1"
b2 is a text with value "A date is a real Otter value, not text. today gives the current date; now gives the current date and time.", size 18, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.55"
b3 is a text with value "date is today\nstarted is now", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b4 is a text with value "A date and a date-time are different", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b5 is a text with value "today has no time of day at all — it is not midnight, it simply does not carry a time. now carries both a date and a time. This is a meaningful distinction, not a technicality: a date with \"no time\" and a date at \"00:00:00\" are not the same idea, so Otter does not pretend one is the other.", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b6 is a text with value "Because of that, asking a plain date for its hour, minute, or second is invalid rather than answering with a silent zero:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b7 is a text with value "date is today\nsay hour of date", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b8 is a text with value "That fails when it runs, with an error explaining that this date has no time of day. Reach for now when you need a time as well as a date.", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b9 is a text with value "Reading the parts of a date", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b10 is a text with value "Date parts are read the same way any other property is read — with of, not with a period. Year, month, and day work on both a date and a date-time:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b11 is a text with value "say year of date\nsay month of date\nsay day of date", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b12 is a text with value "month of date is always a number from 1 to 12, never a month name.", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b13 is a text with value "Hour, minute, and second work on a date-time such as started:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b14 is a text with value "say hour of started\nsay minute of started\nsay second of started", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b15 is a text with value "Adjusting a date", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b16 is a text with value "Move a date forward with add, or backward with remove. Both the singular and plural spelling of a unit are accepted, so 1 day and 7 days both work:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b17 is a text with value "add 7 days to date\nremove 1 month from date", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b18 is a text with value "The same words work on a date-time, down to the second:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b19 is a text with value "add 1 hour to started\nadd 30 minutes to started", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b20 is a text with value "Formatting", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b21 is a text with value "format ... as ... into ... produces text. It does not change the date it was given:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b22 is a text with value "format date as \"MM/dd/yyyy\" into text\nsay text\nsay date", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b23 is a text with value "The second say still prints the original date, untouched.", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b24 is a text with value "The difference between two dates", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b25 is a text with value "days between is an expression, so assign it with the same is form used for every other value:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b26 is a text with value "waiting is days between startDate and endDate\nsay waiting", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b27 is a text with value "The expression can also be used directly wherever a value is expected:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b28 is a text with value "say days between startDate and endDate", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b29 is a text with value "The older days between ... make ... statement remains accepted for compatibility, but new programs should prefer the expression form.", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b30 is a text with value "The result is signed, computed as end minus start:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b31 is a text with value "- positive — endDate is later than startDate", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b32 is a text with value "- zero — the two are the same, at the precision asked for", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b33 is a text with value "- negative — endDate is earlier than startDate", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b34 is a text with value "Comparing dates", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b35 is a text with value "Dates compare with the same words as any other value — there is no separate date-comparison syntax:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b36 is a text with value "if endDate is greater than startDate\n    say \"The end date is later.\"\n.\n\nif date is not started\n    say \"These are different moments.\"\n.", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b37 is a text with value "How a date prints", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b38 is a text with value "say prints a date-only value like this:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b39 is a text with value "say today", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b40 is a text with value "Example output: 2026-09-09", size 15, foreground "#1e3a6b", background "#eaf2ff", radius 12, border "1px solid #cfe0ff", lineheight "1.55", customstyle "padding: 14px 18px;"
b41 is a text with value "and a date-time value like this:", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"
b42 is a text with value "say now", size 14, foreground "#e5edf8", background "#0f1b2e", radius 12, fontfamily "'JetBrains Mono', Consolas, monospace", whitespace "pre", customstyle "padding: 18px 22px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto;"
b43 is a text with value "Example output: 2026-09-09 14:30:05", size 15, foreground "#1e3a6b", background "#eaf2ff", radius 12, border "1px solid #cfe0ff", lineheight "1.55", customstyle "padding: 14px 18px;"
b44 is a text with value "Not part of this version", size 26, weight 800, foreground "#0b1d36", letterspacing "-0.02em", margin "14px 0 0 0"
b45 is a text with value "There is no timezone syntax — a date is always in local time. There is no month-name syntax; month of date is always a number.", size 16, foreground "#3a4d6b", lineheight "1.6"

docsMain is a column with spacing 16, flex 1, padding "40px 56px 24px", customstyle "box-sizing: border-box; min-width: 0; max-width: 940px;"
put b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7, b8, b9, b10, b11, b12, b13, b14, b15, b16, b17, b18, b19, b20, b21, b22, b23, b24, b25, b26, b27, b28, b29, b30, b31, b32, b33, b34, b35, b36, b37, b38, b39, b40, b41, b42, b43, b44, b45 in docsMain
docsBody is a row with align top, spacing 0, width full, customstyle "align-items: stretch;"
put docsSidebar, docsMain in docsBody

put topBar, docsBody, siteFooter in app
show app